<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Erzincan</h1><p class="st-meta">1379 CE – 1410 CE (approx.) · capital Erzincan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The principality of Mutahharten, lord of Erzincan, an ally of Timur on the upper Euphrates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutahharten">Mutahharten</a> was a governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eretnids">Eretnids</a>. As that dynasty collapsed in the late 1370s, he made the city and its fertile plain an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, competing with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kadi-burhan-al-din">Kadi Burhan al-Din</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutahharten">Mutahharten</a> ruled a mixed population of Turks, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> and kept close ties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/empire-of-trebizond">Empire of Trebizond</a>. Threatened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kadi-burhan-al-din">Kadi Burhan al-Din</a> and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, he accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur's</a> overlordship and helped provoke the conflict between Timur and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. The Castilian envoy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruy-gonzalez-de-clavijo">Ruy Gonzalez de Clavijo</a> passed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> in 1404 on his way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutahharten">Mutahharten</a> died around 1403. His successors could not hold out, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> in 1410.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-erzincan.jpg" alt="Emirate of Erzincan" width="320" height="202"><figcaption>Image: Gabagool · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trebizond1400.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1379 CE – 1410 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Erzincan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mutahharten</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mutahharten's emirate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1394&amp;focus=emirate-of-erzincan" aria-label="Emirate of Erzincan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5654 755 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Erzincan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5974 1011L6582 1190M5974 1011L6153 1065"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6582 1190h0M6153 1065h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5974 1011h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5974 1011h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Erzincan. <a href="/atlas?year=1394&amp;focus=emirate-of-erzincan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

